WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:06.388
Telo Ride talks to two companies besides itself: YouTube for video, and Google, with

00:00:06.388 --> 00:00:08.864
your own key, for real-world tiles. Nobody else.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.311
Every response carries a Content Security Policy that says so: scripts, frames,

00:00:15.311 --> 00:00:18.705
images and connections, each with its short list.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.131
A tracker's script, or a call home to anyone else, is refused by the browser before

00:00:28.131 --> 00:00:29.672
it leaves the device.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.594
And every behaviour spec now runs the app under that policy. A single refusal fails

00:00:41.594 --> 00:00:44.920
the spec, so a new third party cannot slip in.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.877
The policy is static: the offline shell is checked by its bytes, so styles stay

00:00:53.877 --> 00:00:56.015
inline, and nothing else does.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.766
Behind it, a sign-in leaves no email, code, token or query string in any span,

00:01:04.766 --> 00:01:06.036
metric or log.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:15.694
Home, under its policy, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.193
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:32.050
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.721
every hill and interval.

00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:39.244
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:44.692
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:47.682
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.520
A custom workout lives under Profile.
